 2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb3690d94ffeJjwww7XwIeuDwQ type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +3ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb3690d94ffeJjwww7XwIeuDwQ sessionID=ses_eb3690d94ffeJjwww7XwIeuDwQ unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/` by reading the code against the tests, but I haven't run the suite. I only had file read/edit tools here, no shell, so I couldn't run `python3 -m unittest`. Tracing each test by hand, they should all pass now.\n\n- **`search.py`**: imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`fees.py`**: added the daily fee to the days late instead of multiplying. It's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`members.py`**: the borrow limit was set to 3, though the policy comment and tests say 5. It's now 5.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n` events, and an empty list if `n <= 0` (otherwise `[-0:]` would return the whole history).\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` stored the year as a string, which also broke `age()`. It now converts it with `int(year)`.\n- **`factory.py`**: the sample data was missing `Emma` (Austen, 1815), so it had two books instead of three.\n\nPlease run `python3 -m unittest` to confirm.INFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +1ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:19:07 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_